course: dictionary
lesson: 5556
title: Lend and lent
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: To lend something means to let someone have it for a while, and they give it back later. «If you lose something a friend lent you, tell them quickly.» Lent is the past tense of lend: the friend gave you the thing earlier.
explain: Lend has more than one meaning. «Lending money to friends can cause arguments» means giving money that must be paid back, sometimes with extra called interest. «Can you lend me a hand?» means can you help me. The words around lend show you which meaning it has.
explain: Context helps you know what is expected. Noah «lent» his best Pokémon card to a kid, and later Noah saw him trading it. The card was not given back, so the kid did not do what a lend promises. You can always say no to lending something.
fact: Lend is a verb. Its forms are lend, lends, lent and lending: «I lent my bike to Sam.»
fact: To lend means to give something for a while, expecting it back.
fact: «Lend a hand» means help, and «lend an ear» means listen.
fact: When a bank lends money, it charges interest, so you pay back more than you borrowed.
fact: A loan is the money or thing that has been lent.
exercise: Your friend lent you a pencil. What did they do? | Hid it under the desk | Took it away for ever | *Gave it to you for a while, expecting it back | Bought it from a shop for you
exercise: «Can you lend me a hand with my bag?» What does lend a hand mean here? | Borrow a hand from someone | *Help | Hold a bag for ever | Clap your hands
exercise: «Some lenders charge huge interest, so £200 borrowed can grow to £400 owed.» What is interest? | *Extra money paid on top of what was borrowed | A bill for a holiday | Money given away for free | A kind of bank card
test: Which sentence uses lend to mean help? | *Can you lend me a hand with my bag? | Can you lend me your bag for an hour? | Can you hand me the bag?
test: Noah lent his card, but the kid kept it. What should Noah do? | Forget about it and never speak to him again | Lend him his whole collection | Throw the card in the bin | *Tell him quickly and ask for the card back
exam: When someone lends you money, what do you usually have to do? | Give it to someone else | *Pay it back, sometimes with interest | Hide it under your bed | Keep it for ever
